      "id": "claim_cdcc5213558f46758dbbfa547de991c9",
      "statement": "Memory pressure shedding is driven by the decision core from allocator-adjusted RSS, the active cgroup working set, and the complete cgroup charge; a node sheds the least-recently-used idle cells, publishes them unowned without resetting their epochs, refuses to reacquire new unowned cells, and does not shed a cell with active work or a live host WebSocket.",
